                <pb facs="0137" n="125" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg125"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/37<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >4/17</hi>: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-10T13:00:00-05:00">June 10, 1940—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>87. With reference to Department’s telegram No. 78, June 1, 1 p.m. Showing
                    himself very emphatically in favor of immediate action President Vincent has
                    just asked most solicitously when Colonels Randolph and Del Valle will
                    arrive.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
